pack.name=Emberlight RTX
pack.description=Ray-traced shadows, GI, reflections, emissive area lights and god rays. Subtle it is not.
option.RTX_INTENSITY=RTX Intensity
option.RTX_INTENSITY.comment=One slider for "more": bloom, glow, gloss, god rays, saturation. 1 = the intended look, 3 = so much.
option.GI_BOUNCES=GI Bounces
option.GI_BOUNCES.comment=Ray-traced diffuse light bounces. 0 = sky and lightmap ambient only.
option.GI_FRAMES=GI History
option.GI_FRAMES.comment=Frames of history the denoiser keeps. More = smoother, slower to react.
option.LIGHT_SAMPLES=Light Candidates
option.LIGHT_SAMPLES.comment=Block lights weighed per pixel each frame; the best one is shared with neighbouring pixels and later frames (ReSTIR). More = cleaner light in rooms full of lamps.
option.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
option.REFLECTIONS.comment=Which surfaces trace reflection rays: Low = mirror-like only, Insane = nearly everything.
value.REFLECTIONS.off=Off
value.REFLECTIONS.low=Low
value.REFLECTIONS.high=High
value.REFLECTIONS.insane=Insane
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Size of the sun disc the shadow rays sample.
option.EMISSIVE_STRENGTH=Emissive Strength
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light Strength
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.VOLUMETRICS=Volumetric Light
option.VOL_STEPS=Volumetric Steps
option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Eye Adaptation
option.WATER_WAVES=Water Waves
option.PUDDLES=Rain Puddles
option.CLOUDS=Clouds
option.PBR_SOURCE=Materials
option.PBR_SOURCE.comment=Auto: LabPBR maps of a resource pack (Emberlight PBR) when present, else the built-in table.
value.PBR_SOURCE.auto=Auto
value.PBR_SOURCE.table=Built-in table
page.lighting=Lighting
page.atmosphere=Atmosphere
page.image=Image
page.quality=Quality
profile.low=Low
profile.medium=Medium
profile.high=High
profile.ultra=Ultra
profile.insane=Insane
option.MIRROR_BOUNCES=Mirror Bounces
option.MIRROR_BOUNCES.comment=Mirrors seen in a mirror reflect on (two facing mirrors: a corridor of images). 1 = other mirrors show as plain colour.
option.NEON_GLOW=Emissive Glow
option.NEON_GLOW.comment=Extra bloom halo around glowing surfaces (lamps, neon terracotta of Emberlight PBR).
option.CAUSTICS=Water Caustics
option.CAUSTICS.comment=Sunlight focused by the waves: dancing light under water and on walls beside it (strongest at sunset). 0 = off.
option.SSS=Subsurface Scattering
option.SSS.comment=Light through leaves and grass when the sun is behind them, soft light on snow, slime and honey. 0 = off.
option.ANISOTROPY=Fog Anisotropy
option.ANISOTROPY.comment=How strongly fog scatters light forward (bright halo toward the sun). 0 = the same in every direction.
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE=Aerial Perspective
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE.comment=Atmospheric haze on distant terrain, from the same atmosphere as the sky. 0 = off.
option.UNDERWATER_RAYS=Underwater Sun Shafts
option.UNDERWATER_RAYS.comment=Ray-traced light shafts through the waves under water (needs volumetric light).
option.SKY_QUALITY=Sky Quality
option.SKY_QUALITY.comment=Ray-march steps of the atmosphere: sky, sunsets, multiple scattering.
option.SUN_INTENSITY=Sun Brightness
option.MOON_INTENSITY=Moon Brightness
option.MOON_INTENSITY.comment=Moonlight also follows the moon phase: full moon brightest, new moon a faint glow.
option.GOLDEN_HOUR=Golden Hour
option.GOLDEN_HOUR.comment=Colour of the low sun: 1 = the atmosphere's own reddening, more = deeper orange, less = whiter.
option.BLUE_HOUR=Blue Hour
option.BLUE_HOUR.comment=Ozone that keeps the twilight sky blue after sunset. 0 = none (orange-grey dusk).
option.POM=Parallax Depth
option.POM.comment=Parallax occlusion mapping from the resource pack's height maps (Emberlight PBR): bricks, cobblestone and planks get real depth up close. Fades out with distance (16 / 32 / 48 blocks).
value.POM.off=Off
value.POM.low=Low
value.POM.high=High
value.POM.ultra=Ultra
option.REFRACTION=Glass and Ice
option.REFRACTION.comment=High: light refracts through glass blocks, ice, slime and honey (traced through the block, tinted by its thickness, total internal reflection) and scatters inside ice, slime and honey. Low: thin tinted sheets.
value.REFRACTION.low=Low
value.REFRACTION.high=High
